{title: 349 - God is Love}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #349 • UBI CARITAS • 8.5.12.12.12.12}
{lyricist: James Quinn}
{composer: A. Gregory Murray}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 349}
{meta: tune UBI CARITAS}
{meta: meter 8.5.12.12.12.12}
{meta: category Christian Church - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]God is love, and [G/B]where true loveis
[Am]God Himself is there.
[F]Here in Christ wegather, [G]love of Christ our call ing.
[Am]Christ, our love, is [F]with us, gladness be His greeting.
[Em]Let usfear Him, yes, and love Him, God eternal.
[Am]Loving Him, let each love [Em]Christ in all his breth ren.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[G]God is love, and where true [C]love is
[C]God Himself is there.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]When we Christians [G/B]gather,
[Am]members of one body,
[Am]Let there be in us no
[F]discord but [G]one spirit.
[Am]Banished [F]now be anger,
[Em]strife, and every quarrel.
[Em]Christ, our God, be always
[Am]present here [Em]among us.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Grant us love's [G/B]fulfillment,
[Am]joy with all the blessed,
[Am]When we see Your face,
[F]O Savior, in [G]its glory.
[Am]Shine on [F]us, O purest
[Em]Light of all creation,
[Em]Be our bliss while endless
[Am]ages sing [Em]Your praises.
{end_of_verse}
